※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4221 LANG_TYPE_TRY_NEEDS_A_RESULT

※ `?` leaves the function carrying the error, so the function must be one that
※ can carry it.  This one answers with a plain number and has nowhere to put
※ an error, so `?` has no meaning in it; `??` is what a function that must not
※ fail uses instead.

let hundred: mut u8 = 100u8
let seven: mut u8 = 7u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    (hundred ÷ seven)?
